{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/962745-violent-feeding","id":962745,"title":"Violent Feeding","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-03T03:01:47-07:00","id":962745,"title":"Violent Feeding","content":"Hi everyone, I'm reading the rules in VtR 2nd ed on page 94 for violent feeding.<br /> <br /> The inset paragraph says that &quot;feed move&quot; may be used &quot;once she has bitten her opponent in a grapple, and bests her opponent in the grapple roll&quot;<br /> <br /> The paragraph under &quot;The Assault, The Kiss&quot; says that vampire fangs are a 0L weapons that use the brawl skill ... while grappling and after a violent bite, the vampire gains access to the feed move.<br /> <br /> On page 177 the grapple rules say you roll Strength + Brawl - Defence to start grappling. There is then a contested roll to actually take the damage action.<br /> <br /> I'm having trouble understanding what this means.<br /> <br /> What is the sequence of events that needs to happen for a vampire to use The Feed Move?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4824-logicalunit","user":"LogicalUnit","date":". 09-03-2016, 06:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4824-logicalunit","name":"LogicalUnit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T03:21:23-07:00","id":962751,"title":"","content":"Okay, I think I've worked it out:<br /> <br /> 1) Grab the opponent with Strength + Brawl - Defence to start grappling<br /> 2) Win a contested Strength + Brawl roll, and choose the Bite/Damage action, which gives you +1 vitae and deals lethal damage to the target (extra +1 for humans), as well as the Scarred condition<br /> 2) Win another contested Strength + Brawl to start Feeding.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4824-logicalunit","name":"LogicalUnit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T05:28:14-07:00","id":962780,"title":"","content":"Your second post is correct. Just to be clear though, those are three separate actions on three separate turns (unless an Exceptional Success was involved somewhere).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T06:20:07-07:00","id":962788,"title":"","content":"Yup. Saibot is right. I just want to add for your 2 ( the first 2 ) that it is +1 vitae PER BLOOD POTENCY up to your successes + 1 extra per vitae taken for humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;She steals one Vitae<br /> per success. Against mortals, this causes one point<br /> of lethal damage per Vitae taken. The number of<br /> Vitae taken may not exceed the vampire\u2019s Blood<br /> Potency dots. &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 09-03-2016, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T07:46:58-07:00","id":962823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/962745-violent-feeding?p=962780#post962780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your second post is correct. Just to be clear though, those are three separate actions on three separate turns (unless an Exceptional Success was involved somewhere).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless in frenzy. Then damage + grapple initiation happen in same round. With exceptional success, damage and feeding can happen simultaneously. Grab-bite-suck them dry like a Fruit Shoot, all while refilling your blood; one of the reasons kindred in a clinch are pretty deadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T04:58:29-07:00","id":963631,"title":"","content":"Related question. Do mortals remember a violent feeding or does The Assault cover it up? Can you lick the bite wound closed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T08:27:22-07:00","id":963704,"title":"","content":"I say, yes they do, but they dont know a vampire bit them and took their blood. They get scared and it's not subtle. I would say you can lick the fang marks, but likely you left a full set of teeth marks behind as you probably caused a lot of damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T09:27:19-07:00","id":963736,"title":"","content":"If I'm not wrong, just with the kiss you are able to lick and heal the wound. I'd not allow with violent feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T10:22:44-07:00","id":963770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/962745-violent-feeding?p=963631#post963631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related question. Do mortals remember a violent feeding or does The Assault cover it up? Can you lick the bite wound closed?</div> </div> </div> </div>First, nothing says the Kiss isn't remembered. It causes some distracting amount of pleasure, so if a vampire is pressed up against you and sucks on your neck you probably won't notice unless you have eyes on your neck. But if you're staring at them while they take your wrist, sink their teeth into it and start drinking, you're going to notice and recognize. The Kiss causes the Swooning Condition, which makes it more difficult to act against them. And during a subtle feeding like the Kiss you can lick the wound closed.<br /> <br /> A violent feeding gives the Scarred Condition and doesn't allow you to lick it closed. In addition, the kine is more susceptible to intimidation and the predatory aura from the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T04:19:16-07:00","id":986040,"title":"","content":"Follow Up: On pg VtR 2nd ed. pg 94, The Feed Move inset says that &quot;She steals one Vitae per success&quot;. On the Storyteller Screen, the Feed action says &quot;Steal one vitae (and inflict one lethal damage)&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which of these is correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4824-logicalunit","name":"LogicalUnit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T04:30:42-07:00","id":986044,"title":"","content":"Both. Taking a Vitae causes one Lethal damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T05:03:00-07:00","id":986055,"title":"","content":"But is it one per success (rulebook) or one in total (storyteller's screen). I'm suspecting it's 1/success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4824-logicalunit","name":"LogicalUnit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T05:27:29-07:00","id":986064,"title":"","content":"It's kind of confusing:<br /> <br /> After you grapple, you have to bite with a Damage move before using the Feed move. This initial bite does damage equal to successes and takes one vitae (this one point of Vitae deals an additional point of Lethal damage to Mortals). After this initial bite, you can use the Feed move. This move takes Successes in Vitae, with each Vitae doing a point of Lethal damage to mortals.<br /> <br /> Any time you take a point of Vitae from mortals, you also deal Lethal damage equal to what was taken.<br /> <br /> So it's one total to initiate the bite and one per success after you've initiated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T05:32:54-07:00","id":986067,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Maina. I wish the rules were more clear -- it's fundamental to the whole Vampire thing. Bite &amp; Feed should be individual grapple moves, available to vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4824-logicalunit","user":"LogicalUnit","date":". 10-12-2016, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4824-logicalunit","name":"LogicalUnit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T06:18:11-07:00","id":986085,"title":"","content":"You can only take 1 vitae per blood potency per turn as well too. So even if you got 5 successes, you can only take 1 vitae, which explains why vampires get blood everywhere when they feed....<br /> On a mortal that would be 6L on a Vampire it would be 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T20:16:44-07:00","id":986535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/962745-violent-feeding?p=986085#post986085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can only take 1 vitae per blood potency per turn as well too. So even if you got 5 successes, you can only take 1 vitae, which explains why vampires get blood everywhere when they feed....<br /> On a mortal that would be 6L on a Vampire it would be 5</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do I still deal 5 lethal damage if I roll 5 successes (and get only 1 vitae)?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I had another read of &quot;The Feed Move&quot;. It says it causes one point of lethal damage per Vitae taken, but the Vitae taken may not exceed the vampire's Blood Potency dots. So the Storyteller's Screen is correct, it just assumes our vampires have only 1 dot of blood potency.<br /> <br /> But now I have another question: does feeding subtly cause lethal damage?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4824-logicalunit","user":"LogicalUnit","date":". 10-12-2016, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4824-logicalunit","name":"LogicalUnit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T02:10:19-07:00","id":986643,"title":"","content":"Yes. <br /> <br /> Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T06:14:27-07:00","id":986711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LogicalUnit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/962745-violent-feeding?p=986535#post986535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do I still deal 5 lethal damage if I roll 5 successes (and get only 1 vitae)?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I had another read of &quot;The Feed Move&quot;. It says it causes one point of lethal damage per Vitae taken, but the Vitae taken may not exceed the vampire's Blood Potency dots. So the Storyteller's Screen is correct, it just assumes our vampires have only 1 dot of blood potency.<br /> <br /> But now I have another question: does feeding subtly cause lethal damage?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Tsusasi is correct. I just want to explain a little where I came up with those numbers, since it seemed a little unclear.<br /> <br /> If you do 5 successes it is 5L but if you are feeding from mortals ( demon's cover, humans, mages, ghouls, ect ) It is an EXTRA 1L per vitae taken and you can take as much as your BP allows. I too assumed you had 1 BP you take 1 vitae from that mortal you do a total of 6L - means you spilled most of that blood everywhere else and only drank down a little...<br /> <br /> Now if you do that same thing to a werewolf or a vampire it is not extra damage as taking vitae from either of those things doesnt actually hurt them. ( or so I was told for werewolf anyway ) You will only do the 5 damage, but get your vitae.<br /> <br /> Even if you are feeding subtly you are draining them of their blood which makes them weak, so it is 1L per vitae taken and you can take as much as their stamina dots. NOT HP track x2 - just stamina dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T06:29:58-07:00","id":986718,"title":"","content":"You can take up to their Health dots.<br /> <br /> Taking more than Stamina dots gives the Drained condition, but you can keep taking more. They'll just likely pass out and have a really nasty Condition to work off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T06:33:08-07:00","id":986719,"title":"","content":"There's nothing that says Werewolves don't take damage from loss of Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T07:13:25-07:00","id":986743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/962745-violent-feeding?p=986718#post986718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can take up to their Health dots.<br /> <br /> Taking more than Stamina dots gives the Drained condition, but you can keep taking more. They'll just likely pass out and have a really nasty Condition to work off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ha! Thank you for my error. Yes. I meant Health dots, not sure why I typed Stamina dots. Good correction!<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> I will be the first to admit, I dont know much about wolves, but I was in 2 different cross over games with wolves and both story tellers said wolves dont take damage from vitae loss, perhaps it was because they arent mortal the way a human is and they are more equivalent to a vampire in that regard. Or perhaps it is because they heal so fast that it wouldnt really affect them the way it would a human. Just speculation though on their reasoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T07:24:50-07:00","id":986748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/962745-violent-feeding?p=986743#post986743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I will be the first to admit, I dont know much about wolves, but I was in 2 different cross over games with wolves and both story tellers said wolves dont take damage from vitae loss, perhaps it was because they arent mortal the way a human is and they are more equivalent to a vampire in that regard. Or perhaps it is because they heal so fast that it wouldnt really affect them the way it would a human. Just speculation though on their reasoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I think I see where they're getting that interpretation from. The Feed Move sidebar says, &quot;Against mortals, this causes one point of lethal damage per Vitae taken&quot; and later under <i>The Assault, The Kiss</i> it says, &quot;In reference to the effects of a bite, the word \u201cmortal\u201d applies to humans, ghouls, warlocks, and other things that are mostly human. Vampires, werewolves, mummies, fairies, and other things far removed from humanity are not normally subject to the Assault and the Kiss.&quot; I'm pretty sure this is supposed to refer specifically to the Swooning and Scarred Conditions, and that The Feed Move sidebar is using &quot;mortals&quot; to mean &quot;non-vampires.&quot; But, I can see how it could be interpreted as saying werewolves don't take lethal from the Feed move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T15:30:21-07:00","id":986978,"title":"","content":"Werewolves still need blood to live though :P Is just common sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T23:18:21-07:00","id":987639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/962745-violent-feeding?p=986643#post986643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.<br /> <br /> Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure, after re-reading the rules on pg 94.<br /> <br /> I believe we can all agree that violent feeding starts with a grapple. This is Strength + Brawl - Defence roll. On success, the vampire is grappling with his target.<br /> <br /> The next step is to bite. Page 94 and page 177 describe a vampire's fangs as +0 lethal weapons, that can be used as part of a Damage move during a grapple. This means the vampire needs to win an opposed Strength + Brawl roll. The vampire deals lethal damage to the target equal to the number of succeses, and also takes one vitae (which deals an additional point of lethal damage to mortals).<br /> <br /> Once the target has been bitten, the vampire gains access the to Feed move. This requires another contested Strength + Brawl roll. If successful, the vampire steals one vitae per success, and causes one point of lethal damage per vitae taken -- but the vitae taken MAY NOT EXCEED THE VAMPIRE'S BLOOD POTENCY DOTS. <br /> <br /> Most vampires start with 1 dot of blood potency. It can be increased by spending 5 dots worth of Merits.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for non-violent or subtle feeding, where does it say it causes lethal damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4824-logicalunit","name":"LogicalUnit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T03:13:34-07:00","id":987691,"title":"","content":"Page 95, &quot;Blood Supplies,&quot; under Human Blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every point of Vitae she takes causes one point of lethal damage. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T03:24:54-07:00","id":987692,"title":"","content":"Cool, thanks for pointing that out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4824-logicalunit","name":"LogicalUnit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}